/*
 * Copyright 2026 NXP
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: mark which SoC power states stop this CTIMER
 * counting. Stacked on top of whatever the board target already applies, for the
 * system layer only (via EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE).
 *
 * Every board target in platform_allow gets this list from its SoC dtsi, for every
 * CTIMER instance rather than just ctimer0, so this restates what is already there.
 * It is kept so the system layer does not depend on those dtsi commits being in the
 * tree: on a checkout without them, this is what supplies the list.
 *
 * All three states are listed because every MCXN and MCXA board this case runs on
 * attaches PLL0, or the equivalent system PLL, to its CTIMER and that PLL is off in
 * all three. Per MCX Nx4x RM Rev. 6_RC2 Table 336 the block itself is "LP/Static" in
 * Deep Sleep and Power Down, so what stops the counter there is the clock and not
 * the block.
 *
 * Deep Power Down additionally gates the CORE domain and resets the registers.
 */

&ctimer0 {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&deepsleep &powerdown &deeppowerdown>;
};
